    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-warmup-actions-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Say who does what",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put the person or people first, then the action, then its object. Recombine independently introduced actions and objects in this order. The verb keeps the same form when the person changes. 和 joins people; 也 goes before the action to mean also.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我和你学中文。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ hé nǐ xué Zhōngwén 。",
                "meaning": "You and I study Chinese.",
                "audio": "09f0f518040839dcb3832ea55676fe15c4e373c94b7946fbb92a5102e639bb47"
              },
              {
                "text": "我也学中文。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yě xué Zhōngwén 。",
                "meaning": "I study Chinese too.",
                "audio": "8fb6c1f5c1ae40060c409548d1dd08b75e73899da24a4a1d6f4e54076403f1e5"
              }
            ]
          },
